  "id": "stem-and-leaf-plot",
  "term": "stem-and-leaf plot",
  "definition": "A stem-and-leaf plot is a simple display of numerical data in which each value is split into a stem and a leaf, usually with all but the last digit forming the stem and the last digit forming the leaf. The stems are listed vertically with matching leaves beside them, making small data sets easy to inspect while still preserving the original values.",
